WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.362
"We have to find the dungeon!" Gliss exclaimed.

2
00:00:03.363 --> 00:00:05.928
"That's where my parents are being held!"

3
00:00:05.929 --> 00:00:11.490
"I know," Darb said calmly. "But there's no sense rushing into the dungeon on our own.

4
00:00:11.491 --> 00:00:16.503
We should find our friends first, and then look for it together. That was the plan."

5
00:00:16.504 --> 00:00:24.645
Gliss gritted her teeth, feeling frustrated. She and Darb had been arguing ever since she'd zapped them away ten minutes earlier.

6
00:00:24.646 --> 00:00:28.694
"Why are you being so unbelievably stubborn?" she cried.

7
00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.821
She was so exasperated that she poked him in the chest.

8
00:00:31.822 --> 00:00:36.445
To her surprise, Darb reached out and gave her a hard shove in return.

9
00:00:36.446 --> 00:00:43.550
"Hey!" she blurted out in surprise as she stumbled backward and onto the floor. "How dare you—"

10
00:00:43.551 --> 00:00:46.175
"Shh!" said Darb.

11
00:00:46.176 --> 00:00:49.375
Just then Gliss felt something whiz past her head.

12
00:00:49.376 --> 00:00:53.939
"Stay down!" Darb cried, flinging himself to the floor beside her.

13
00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:54.812
Thud!

14
00:00:54.813 --> 00:00:58.831
Gliss heard the thing hit the wall at the end of the hallway.

15
00:00:58.832 --> 00:01:03.093
Then she ducked her head as another whizzing object shot over them.

16
00:01:03.094 --> 00:01:08.264
"What was that?" she yelped. "Is someone shooting arrows at us?"

17
00:01:08.265 --> 00:01:12.426
"I don't think they're arrows!" Darb pointed toward the end of the hall.

18
00:01:12.427 --> 00:01:15.772
Gliss saw a long, narrow creature hanging there.

19
00:01:15.773 --> 00:01:19.616
It looked like some kind of lizard with suction cups for feet.

20
00:01:19.617 --> 00:01:25.653
As she watched, it pulled its snout out from the stone wall, revealing a sharp blade.

21
00:01:25.654 --> 00:01:29.757
Pushing off with its feet, the lizard hurled itself straight at them again.

22
00:01:29.758 --> 00:01:34.059
"Ah!" Gliss cried, rolling to the side just in time.

23
00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:38.743
"Sorry I shoved you," Darb said breathlessly. "There was no time to—"

24
00:01:38.744 --> 00:01:41.701
Three more of the creatures sailed past them.

25
00:01:41.702 --> 00:01:52.630
"I know," Gliss said. "And now it's my turn to save you." She grabbed his hand. "Zap!"

26
00:01:52.631 --> 00:01:58.639
Zann grasped his grandfather's hands through the bars, feeling happier than he had in days.

27
00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.235
"Are you sure you're okay?" he asked.

28
00:02:02.236 --> 00:02:08.698
Boz chuckled, squeezing Zann's hands. "I'm fine," he said.

29
00:02:08.699 --> 00:02:14.323
"Luckily, I haven't been a victim of Morb's leech treatment for a couple of days."

30
00:02:14.324 --> 00:02:18.022
"Nor have I," said Teplo from the next cell.

31
00:02:18.023 --> 00:02:21.787
"I'm starting to think Morb ran out of those nasty creatures."

32
00:02:21.788 --> 00:02:27.773
Zann was happy to hear that Boz and Teplo were okay. But some of the other Reds in the dungeon looked weak and ill.

33
00:02:27.774 --> 00:02:30.483
The king and queen were sharing a cell nearby.

34
00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:34.225
Both were slumped on the floor, pale and shaking.

35
00:02:34.226 --> 00:02:37.426
Zann also spotted several other familiar faces.

36
00:02:37.427 --> 00:02:41.277
The mayor of Swamp Bottom was a few cells from the king and queen.

37
00:02:41.278 --> 00:02:44.404
Gliss' parents were huddled together farther down the aisle.

38
00:02:44.405 --> 00:02:47.714
Some of Boz's other Magic Master friends were there too.

39
00:02:47.715 --> 00:02:52.788
"I've got to get you all out of here," Zann said. He glanced at Teplo.

40
00:02:52.789 --> 00:02:58.735
"Fala is here—some other people too—and everyone is ready to fight Morb."

41
00:02:58.736 --> 00:03:03.673
"Ah, you've raised a brave boy, Boz!" Teplo said with a smile.

42
00:03:03.674 --> 00:03:10.545
Zann rubbed his hands together and pointed at the huge metal lock on Boz's cell door. "Open," he said.

43
00:03:10.546 --> 00:03:14.887
Nothing happened. "Don't bother, Zann," Boz said.

44
00:03:14.888 --> 00:03:19.413
"Morb has put a Dousing spell over the entire dungeon."

45
00:03:19.414 --> 00:03:25.390
"That's right," Teplo added wryly. "Do you think we would have stuck around if we'd had a choice?"

46
00:03:25.391 --> 00:03:31.413
Zann's shoulders slumped. He'd just regained his magic, and now it was useless again.

47
00:03:31.414 --> 00:03:36.854
"Without magic, how am I supposed to . . ." His words trailed off.

48
00:03:36.855 --> 00:03:44.050
He could almost hear Darb's voice in his head: It is possible to get into a house without magic, you know!

49
00:03:44.051 --> 00:03:50.826
Zann grinned. Any door that could be opened with magic could also be opened without it.

50
00:03:50.827 --> 00:03:54.870
He stepped away from the cells and scanned the walls near the steps.

51
00:03:54.871 --> 00:03:57.985
The item he needed should be here somewhere . . .

52
00:03:57.986 --> 00:04:03.585
"Aha!" said Zann. He reached over and grabbed a key off a hook on the wall.

53
00:04:03.586 --> 00:04:07.440
It was inside the stairwell, just out of sight of the prisoners.

54
00:04:07.441 --> 00:04:09.970
Boz's eyes widened when he saw it.

55
00:04:09.971 --> 00:04:16.183
"Good thinking, my boy! Now hurry and get us out of here!"

56
00:04:16.184 --> 00:04:20.238
Morb rubbed his fingers together and touched the talisman in his hand.

57
00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:26.127
Energy emanated from it and flowed through the air and into the talismans of the trolls standing in front of him.

58
00:04:26.128 --> 00:04:31.437
Morb hated to give up that magical energy, especially when he had so little left.

59
00:04:31.438 --> 00:04:39.009
But he couldn't risk leaving the palace without strong trolls to guard him—especially not now, when he was so close to victory.

60
00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:41.870
"Come with me," Morb ordered the trolls.

61
00:04:41.871 --> 00:04:44.877
They marched behind him as he walked through the palace.

62
00:04:44.878 --> 00:04:51.532
The blob Wyssa had brought last week was still guarding the entrance, but it shrank back respectfully as Morb passed.

63
00:04:51.533 --> 00:04:59.265
Morb strode across the square, ignoring the few citizens that were scurrying about. Soon he reached the riverbank.

64
00:04:59.266 --> 00:05:02.503
"I should find what I need here," he muttered.

65
00:05:02.504 --> 00:05:06.542
Rubbing his hands together, Morb focused on the river before him.

66
00:05:06.543 --> 00:05:09.330
"Levitate!" he intoned.

67
00:05:09.331 --> 00:05:17.110
Energy sizzled from Morb's hands. With a groan the entire riverbank rose, dripping water and dirt.

68
00:05:17.111 --> 00:05:22.013
Morb waved a hand, and the mass moved until it was directly over him.

69
00:05:22.014 --> 00:05:27.603
The trolls stepped back, staring fearfully up at the huge chunk of earth hanging overhead.

70
00:05:27.604 --> 00:05:34.794
Morb smiled as his sharp amber eyes spotted a small, gray shape wriggling out of the dirt above him.

71
00:05:34.795 --> 00:05:40.765
Just as he'd expected, the leeches had burrowed into the riverbank as soon as they'd felt his spell.

72
00:05:40.766 --> 00:05:45.069
Now they had burrowed straight through and were falling from the bottom.

73
00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:48.489
Morb reached out and caught the first leech as it fell.

74
00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:54.004
Then he turned away, ignoring the dozens of others that were raining down around him.

75
00:05:54.005 --> 00:06:03.080
"That's all," he told the trolls. "Let's go."

